<main class="write-main ux-workflow"><header class="ux-page-heading"><p class="ux-eyebrow">Audience and discovery</p><h1>SEO publishing checks</h1><p>Review the content you control, then use Search Console for actual search and indexing evidence. These checks are not ranking guarantees or invented traffic scores.</p><div class="ux-next-actions"><a href="<?=url('/write/discovery')?>">Search performance</a><a href="<?=url('/write/google')?>">Google connection diagnostics</a><a href="<?=url('/publishing-sitemap.xml')?>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Public publishing sitemap</a></div></header><section class="ux-card"><h2>Technical foundations</h2><p>Public pages use canonical URLs, visible navigation and breadcrumbs. Public monthly editions join the publishing sitemap; private forms, client workspaces and unpublished records do not. Sponsored links retain their disclosure and sponsored relationship attribute.</p><p>JavaScript improves navigation without replacing the original content or crawlable links. Public content is readable without scripts, and private form details stay outside public metadata.</p></section><section class="ux-card"><h2>Latest public article sample · <?=count($checks)?> of up to 200</h2><p>Focus on useful first-hand content, distinct titles, accurate summaries and meaningful image descriptions. Suggested title length is an editorial prompt, not a search-engine rule.</p><div class="ux-table-scroll"><table data-ux-filter-table><thead><tr><th>Article</th><th>Review prompts</th><th>Next action</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($checks as$c):?><tr><td><a href="<?=e($c['url'])?>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><?=e($c['title'])?></a></td><td><?=e($c['notes']?implode(' ',$c['notes']):'No issues in these limited field checks.')?></td><td><a href="<?=url('/write/edit/'.$c['id'])?>">Edit draft</a></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div><?php if(!$checks):?><p>No published articles were returned for this sample. This is not evidence of indexing or ranking.</p><?php endif;?></section></main>
